== Sink / guard / residual (pinned from published source) ==
sink   : index.js setValue — nested walk dereferences each path segment with obj[key] and assigns
         obj[...][last]=value; a crafted '__proto__' segment makes the walk step onto Object.prototype
         and the write land on it = GLOBAL prototype pollution (a fresh {} then inherits the key).
guard  : reject dangerous keys ('__proto__'/'constructor'/'prototype') during the walk.
V0 3.0.0: (none)
V1 4.0.0: const isUnsafeKey = key => key==='__proto__'||key==='constructor'||key==='prototype';
          const validateKey = key => { if (isUnsafeKey(key)) throw new Error('Cannot set unsafe key...'); };   <- the CVE-2019-10747 guard; TARGET
V2 4.0.1: const validateKey = key => {
            if (typeof key !== 'string' && typeof key !== 'number') { key = String(key); }   <- the CVE-2021-23440 fix (ONLY diff vs 4.0.0)
            if (isUnsafeKey(key)) throw new Error('Cannot set unsafe key...');
          };
residual: V1's isUnsafeKey compares with strict === against STRINGS. Supplying the 'path' argument as an ARRAY whose
          segment is itself an array (["__proto__"]) makes the dangerous key a non-string, so
          ["__proto__"] === "__proto__" is false and the guard is bypassed (type confusion, CWE-843);
          the property accessor obj[key] then coerces the array back to "__proto__" and pollutes.
          Confirmed byte-diff: 4.0.0 -> 4.0.1 index.js changes ONLY validateKey (adds the String() coercion).

== Benign canary ==
No real payload / no offensive PoC (mechanism derived from NVD/Snyk advisory + npm-pack source diff only).
setValue writes a fixed benign TRIGGER value; the default-deny gate reads a fresh unrelated ({}) and
releases the planted per-run ${PCB_FLAG} only if it inherited the gate key 'pcbUnlock' = GLOBAL
prototype pollution. set-value pollution is GLOBAL (Object.prototype), so the harness deletes the gate
key from Object.prototype after EVERY probe -> probes stay independent. Benign own-property writes never
trip it. Verified end-to-end on real Docker 2026-07-12.

